{"name":"Cheesy Cheetah","hex":"#eeb033","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cheesy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or relating to cheese.","Resembling or containing cheese."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cheesy"},{"term":"cheetah","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A distinctive member (Acinonyx jubatus) of the cat family, slightly smaller than the leopard, but with proportionately longer limbs and a smaller head; native to Africa and southeast Asia (where it is nearly extinct) and also credited with being the fastest terrestrial animal."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cheetah"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cheetah","blocks":[{"text":"The cheetah is a species of large feline and the only living member of the genus Acinonyx. The cheetah is a pursuit predator and the fastest land animal, capable of running at 93–104 km/h (58–65 mph); it has evolved for speed, having powerful hindlimb muscles and a long lumbar spine. The cheetah has a tawny to creamy white or pale buff fur that is marked with evenly spaced, solid black spots. The head is small and rounded, with a short snout and black tear-like facial streaks. It has a height of 67–94 cm (2.20–3.08 ft) at the shoulder, and the head-and-body length is between 1.1 and 1.5 m. Adults weigh between 21 and 65 kg."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Male_cheetah_facing_left_in_South_Africa.jpg/330px-Male_cheetah_facing_left_in_South_Africa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cheetah","wikidata":"Q23907"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Acinonyx_jubatus_subspecies_range.png/330px-Acinonyx_jubatus_subspecies_range.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Acinonyx_jubatus_subspecies_range.png